{
  "thought_process": "I looked up your account and verified the line and plan details first. Your line ending in 2002 is Active, international roaming on our side is already enabled, and you still have data left in your plan (so you aren’t throttled due to hitting the cap). That means the most likely causes are device-side settings while roaming (roaming/Data/Network mode/Data Saver/VPN/Wi‑Fi interactions) or a temporary network condition in your area. We’ll run a few quick diagnostics and a refresh to restore fast roaming data, then measure with a speed test. If the serving 5G cell is congested, we’ll compare 5G vs 4G to get you the best ‘excellent’ speed available.",
  "account_check_summary": {
    "customer_id": "C1001",
    "line_id": "L1002",
    "phone_number": "555-123-2002",
    "line_status": "Active",
    "roaming_enabled_on_account": true,
    "plan": {
      "plan_id": "P1002",
      "name": "Premium Plan",
      "data_limit_gb": 15,
      "refuel_price_per_gb": 2
    },
    "current_cycle_usage": {
      "used_gb": 8.7,
      "remaining_gb": 6.3,
      "cycle_end_date": "2025-02-28"
    }
  },
  "what_we_will_do_now": "Let’s run two quick diagnostics to see your current connection state, then do a fast refresh and measure speed.",
  "steps_for_you_now": [
    {
      "step": "Diagnostic 1 — Check status bar",
      "why": "Confirms signal strength, network type (5G/4G), and whether anything like Airplane Mode, Wi‑Fi, Data Saver, or VPN might be affecting data.",
      "how": "Look at the top status bar and note: signal bars, network type (5G/4G/LTE/3G/2G), Wi‑Fi icon (on/off), airplane icon (on/off), data saver icon, and VPN key/lock if present.",
      "what_to_report_back": "Please tell me: number of signal bars (0–4), network type shown, and whether you see icons for Wi‑Fi, Airplane Mode, Data Saver, or VPN."
    },
    {
      "step": "Diagnostic 2 — Check network status in settings",
      "why": "Verifies that Mobile Data is ON and Data Roaming is ON on the phone itself (in addition to being enabled on your line).",
      "how": "On your phone: Settings > Mobile Network/Cellular > ensure Mobile Data is ON. Then go to Mobile Data Options/Cellular Data Options and ensure Data Roaming is ON.",
      "what_to_report_back": "Confirm whether Mobile Data is ON and Data Roaming is ON."
    },
    {
      "step": "Quick refresh",
      "why": "Forces a clean re-registration on the local network, which often restores full-speed data while roaming.",
      "how": "Turn Wi‑Fi OFF temporarily. Then turn Airplane Mode ON for 10 seconds and turn it OFF again. Wait 30–45 seconds for 4G/5G to reappear.",
      "what_to_report_back": "After the refresh, what network type shows (5G/4G) and how many bars do you see?"
    },
    {
      "step": "Speed test",
      "why": "We need to quantify performance and confirm it’s at an ‘excellent’ level.",
      "how": "With Wi‑Fi still OFF, please run a speed test (any speed test app or your browser speed test).",
      "what_to_report_back": "Share the download speed result (or if it says no connection)."
    }
  ],
  "next_if_needed": [
    "If speed isn’t excellent, we’ll set Preferred network to 4G/5G preferred. If it’s already set, we’ll test switching temporarily to 4G-only to compare—this can outperform a congested 5G cell.",
    "We’ll also ensure Data Saver is OFF and any VPN is OFF, then, if needed, reset APN to default and reboot to apply clean roaming settings.",
    "You still have 6.3 GB available this cycle; if you ever need more, I can refuel up to 2 GB at $2/GB instantly."
  ],
  "please_reply_with": {
    "diagnostic_1": "Status bar details (signal bars, 5G/4G label, Wi‑Fi/Plane/Data Saver/VPN icons)",
    "diagnostic_2": "Whether Mobile Data and Data Roaming are ON in settings",
    "post_refresh": "Network type and bars after the Airplane Mode refresh",
    "speed_test": "Speed result or ‘no connection’"
  }
}

