messages.content:
{
  "response": "I can help. Here’s my plan and why: 1) Identify your line to check for any account/line issues (like data cap reached or roaming not enabled). 2) Walk you through quick on‑device checks that commonly cause slow/no mobile data (airplane mode, mobile data switch, Data Saver, VPN, network mode, APN). We’ll aim to restore excellent speeds if conditions allow. First, please help me identify your account: • What’s the phone number for the line with the issue? (Or provide your customer ID, or your full name + date of birth.) A few quick questions to narrow it down: • Are you currently traveling outside your usual service area/country? • Does the problem happen everywhere you go or only in a specific location? • When did it start? • What phone model are you using? While I look up your line, please run these fast checks on your phone and share the results: 1) Check status bar: Make sure you do NOT see Airplane Mode; confirm you see signal bars and a network type like 4G/LTE/5G, and that mobile data is enabled. (Use: check_status_bar or check_network_status.) 2) Speed test: Run run_speed_test and tell me the result (we classify Excellent as the target; anything lower helps me diagnose). 3) Data Saver: Check if Data Saver is ON. If it is, turn it OFF (check_data_restriction_status, then toggle_data_saver_mode). 4) VPN: If a VPN is connected, disconnect it (check_vpn_status, then disconnect_vpn) because it can severely slow data. 5) Network mode: Ensure your phone prefers modern networks (set to 4g_5g_preferred) rather than 2G/3G (check_network_mode_preference; if needed, set_network_mode_preference). 6) APN sanity check: If speeds are still poor or data drops, check APN settings (check_apn_settings). If they look incorrect, reset to default and then reboot your phone (reset_apn_settings, then reboot_device). Once I have your phone number, I’ll also: • Check your current data usage vs. plan limit and refuel data if you’ve hit the cap. • Verify roaming is enabled on your line if you’re traveling and enable it if needed at no cost. Please share your line’s phone number and the results of steps 1–2 to start."
}

