{
  "message": "I can help you get service back. Here’s the plan: I’ll look up your line to rule out any account-related causes (like a suspension), while you run a few quick checks on the phone to isolate device/network issues. Doing both in parallel is the fastest way to restore service.",
  "need_customer_identification": "To start the account check, please provide ONE of the following: (a) the phone number on the affected line, OR (b) your customer ID, OR (c) your full name AND date of birth (YYYY-MM-DD).",
  "quick_questions": [
    "Are you currently traveling outside your usual area or abroad?",
    "Did anything change recently (new SIM/phone, port-in, plan change, or a recent bill/payment issue you’re aware of)?",
    "Do other lines on your account (if any) have service right now?"
  ],
  "phone_checks": [
    {
      "step": "Check the status bar",
      "why": "Confirms whether Airplane Mode or lack of signal is the cause.",
      "how": "Look at the top of the screen. Tell me exactly what you see (e.g., ✈️ Airplane Mode, 📵 No Signal/No Service, 5G/LTE, Wi‑Fi, battery)."
    },
    {
      "step": "Toggle Airplane Mode",
      "why": "Resets all radios and often restores network registration.",
      "how": "Turn Airplane Mode ON, wait 10 seconds, then turn it OFF. After it turns off, wait 30–60 seconds and see if signal bars return."
    },
    {
      "step": "Check SIM status",
      "why": "A missing or locked SIM will cause No Service.",
      "how": "Settings > About phone (or Connections) > SIM status. Tell me if it shows Active, Missing, or Locked. If Missing and you have a physical SIM, power off, remove and reinsert the SIM carefully, then power on. If it shows Locked (PIN/PUK), stop and tell me—don’t try random codes."
    },
    {
      "step": "Preferred network mode",
      "why": "If set to an old mode (2G/3G), service can fail.",
      "how": "Settings > Mobile network/Cellular network > Preferred network type. Set it to 4G/5G preferred."
    },
    {
      "step": "Reboot the phone",
      "why": "Clears temporary glitches and forces a fresh network registration.",
      "how": "Restart/power off and back on, then wait 1–2 minutes for signal."
    }
  ],
  "what_i_will_do_next": "Once you share your identification, I will verify your line’s status (active vs. suspended), check for any overdue-bill-related holds, and confirm roaming eligibility if you’re traveling. If I find a suspension due to billing, I’ll guide you to clear it and immediately resume the line.",
