messages.content:
{
  "message": "Thanks for the update. Since your phone shows “No SIM” and “No Signal,” MMS (and all cellular services) can’t work until the SIM is detected. This points to a SIM recognition issue rather than a network/roaming issue. Let’s confirm the SIM status and try a reseat, then reboot. I’ll also outline what to do based on the result.",
  "my_thought_process": [
    "Your line is Active and roaming is now enabled on our side, and you still have data left. The phone reporting “SIM missing” means the device isn’t detecting the SIM/eSIM, which must be fixed first.",
    "Most often, reseating the SIM and rebooting resolves this. If it’s an eSIM, we’ll confirm whether the eSIM profile is active; if it shows Locked (PIN/PUK), we’ll escalate."
  ],
  "quick_questions": [
    "Is your line using a physical SIM card or an eSIM on this Android phone?",
    "Did anything happen recently that could affect the SIM (SIM tray removed/swapped, device drop, water exposure)?"
  ],
  "steps_now": [
    {
      "title": "1) Check the SIM status",
      "steps": [
        "On your phone, check the SIM status (Settings > About phone > SIM status if available) or use your device’s diagnostics to confirm it reports Missing/Active/Locked.",
        "Tell me exactly what it shows (Missing, Active, or Locked)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "2) If it says Missing: Reseat the SIM, then reboot",
      "reason": "A slightly misaligned SIM can cause intermittent or complete loss of detection.",
      "steps": [
        "Power the phone OFF completely.",
        "Remove the SIM tray with the tool/paperclip. Carefully take out the SIM.",
        "Inspect the SIM and tray: ensure the gold contacts are clean and the SIM isn’t cracked or bent.",
        "Reinsert the SIM in the correct orientation and fully seat the tray.",
        "Power the phone ON.",
        "Wait 1–2 minutes and check the status bar for signal bars or a carrier name.",
        "Check the SIM status again (Active/Missing/Locked) and let me know which it shows."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "3) If it says Locked (after reboot)",
      "reason": "This indicates a SIM PIN/PUK lock. We’ll need to unlock it before service can resume.",
      "steps": [
        "Do not attempt random PIN/PUK entries.",
        "Tell me it shows Locked and I’ll escalate to provide proper SIM security assistance."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "4) If you use eSIM (no physical SIM)",
      "steps": [
        "Reboot the device first (power OFF, then ON).",
        "After reboot, check whether the SIM status changes from Missing to Active.",
        "If it still shows Missing, tell me—it may require re-provisioning the eSIM profile, which I can arrange."
      ]
    }
  ],
  "what_to_do_after_success": [
    "If the SIM status becomes Active and you see signal bars: keep Wi‑Fi OFF, ensure Mobile data and Data roaming are ON, then try loading a web page (example.com). If browsing works, try sending a small MMS photo to one contact.",
    "If MMS still fails after SIM is detected and data works, we’ll continue with APN reset + reboot and Wi‑Fi Calling OFF as previously outlined."
  ],
  "next_info_i_need_from_you": [
    "Is your setup physical SIM or eSIM?",
    "What does the SIM status show right now (Missing, Active, or Locked) after following the steps above?"
  ]
}

