messages.content:
{
  "message": "Great—your SIM is now detected, you have strong 5G signal, and mobile data works. That means MMS is likely being blocked by a phone configuration issue (Wi‑Fi Calling interaction, APN/MMSC settings, app permissions, Data Saver, or VPN). Let’s work through the MMS‑specific fixes now.",
  "my_thought_process": [
    "MMS requires mobile data plus a correct MMSC (part of APN).",
    "Wi‑Fi Calling can sometimes interfere with MMS; turning it OFF helps isolate.",
    "If APN/MMSC is wrong or stale, resetting APN and rebooting usually fixes it.",
    "The Messages app must have Storage/Media and SMS permissions. Data Saver/VPN can also block it."
  ],
  "steps": [
    {
      "title": "1) Turn OFF Wi‑Fi Calling (temporarily) and test",
      "why": "Some networks don’t support MMS over Wi‑Fi Calling.",
      "do": [
        "Settings > Network & Internet (or Connections) > Mobile network > Wi‑Fi Calling > turn OFF.",
        "With Wi‑Fi still OFF and Mobile data ON, try sending a small photo (MMS) to a single contact."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "2) Reset APN settings to default, then reboot",
      "why": "Ensures a correct MMSC is set for MMS.",
      "do": [
        "Settings > Network & Internet (or Connections) > Mobile network > Access Point Names.",
        "Tap the menu (⋮) > Reset to default.",
        "Restart the phone.",
        "After reboot, keep Wi‑Fi OFF, Mobile data + Data roaming ON, and try sending a small MMS again."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "3) Confirm Messages app permissions",
      "why": "Without Storage/Media and SMS permissions, MMS can fail.",
      "do": [
        "Settings > Apps > Messages (your default messaging app) > Permissions.",
        "Allow: SMS/Messages and Photos and videos (Storage/Media).",
        "Return and test sending a small MMS."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "4) Turn OFF Data Saver and any VPN, then test",
      "why": "Data Saver can restrict data; VPNs can interfere with MMS delivery.",
      "do": [
        "Settings > Network & Internet > Data Saver > turn OFF.",
        "Settings > Network & Internet > VPN > disconnect any active VPN.",
        "Optional: Ensure per‑app background data is allowed for Messages (Settings > Apps > Messages > Mobile data & Wi‑Fi > Allow background data usage ON).",
        "Test sending a small MMS again."
      ]
    }
  ],
  "what_i_need_from_you": [
    "After Step 1: Did MMS send with Wi‑Fi Calling OFF?",
    "If not, after Step 2 (APN reset + reboot): Did MMS send?",
    "If still not, confirm you granted the two permissions in Step 3 and that Data Saver/VPN are OFF from Step 4, then tell me exactly what happens when you send (e.g., still spinning then fails, any new error message)."
  ],
  "notes": [
    "Keep Wi‑Fi OFF while testing MMS so it uses mobile data.",
    "Once MMS works, you can turn Wi‑Fi back ON. We can also re‑enable Wi‑Fi Calling if needed and re‑test."
  ]
}

