{
  "message": "Thanks for the update. Since mobile data is working and Wi‑Fi Calling is OFF, the most likely remaining blocker is the messaging app’s media permission or an app-level data restriction. Let’s grant the correct permissions and double-check the app’s data settings, then try one more network-mode tweak.",
  "thought_process": "MMS needs mobile data (confirmed OK), a valid MMSC (confirmed present), and the messaging app’s permissions (SMS + media). If the app lacks Photos/Media (or Storage) permission, MMS can fail. Some Android versions label this as “Photos and videos” or “Files and media,” and it may appear under Not allowed. We’ll enable it and ensure the app can use data in the background. If it still fails, we’ll test on 4G-only to rule out a radio quirk. After that, if MMS still won’t send, it likely needs a backend MMS re‑provision.",
  "steps": [
    {
      "title": "Identify your default SMS app (confirm)",
      "do_this": [
        "Settings > Apps > Default apps > SMS app.",
        "Confirm the name is exactly: messaging."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Grant media/storage permission to the messaging app",
      "why": "MMS requires access to media files.",
      "android": [
        "Settings > Apps > messaging > Permissions.",
        "Look under Allowed and Not allowed for any of these permission names and set to Allow:",
        "- Photos and videos,",
        "- Files and media,",
        "- Storage.",
        "If you don’t see these under the app’s Permissions:",
        "Settings > Privacy > Permission manager > Photos and videos (or Files and media/Storage) > find messaging > set to Allow."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Ensure the app can use mobile data",
      "do_this": [
        "Settings > Apps > messaging > Mobile data & Wi‑Fi (or Data usage).",
        "Turn ON ‘Allow background data usage’.",
        "Turn ON ‘Allow data usage while Data Saver is on’ (if present)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Test MMS",
      "do_this": [
        "Keep Wi‑Fi OFF and Mobile data ON.",
        "Open the messaging app and try sending an MMS again.",
        "Note exactly what happens (e.g., sends successfully or shows Not sent)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "If still failing: try 4G/LTE only (temporary test)",
      "do_this": [
        "Settings > Mobile network > Preferred network type.",
        "Select 4G/LTE only.",
        "Wait ~20 seconds and try sending an MMS again."
      ]
    }
  ],
  "what_to_report_back": [
    "Were you able to find and Allow a media permission (Photos and videos / Files and media / Storage) for the messaging app?",
    "Is background data allowed for the messaging app?",
    "After these changes, did the MMS send?",
