messages.content:
{
  "acknowledgement": "Thanks for the update. “No Signal” + “Data Disabled” means the phone isn’t connected to the cellular network at all, so MMS will fail. The most common causes are: Airplane Mode ON, a SIM card issue (missing/loose/locked), or the radio stuck on an unsuitable network mode. We’ll refresh the radio, verify the SIM, and ensure the right network mode.",
  "plan": "Please follow the steps below in order and share the exact results. I’m explaining why each step matters.",
  "steps": [
    {
      "step": "Check and reset Airplane Mode",
      "why": "Airplane Mode disables all cellular radios and will show No Signal/Data Disabled.",
      "instructions": [
        "Open Settings > Network/Connections.",
        "If Airplane Mode is ON, turn it OFF.",
        "If it’s already OFF, toggle it ON, wait 10 seconds, then turn it OFF again.",
        "Wait ~15 seconds and watch the status bar for signal bars and 4G/LTE/5G."
      ],
      "tell_me": [
        "After toggling, do you still see “No Signal”?",
        "Do you see any bars or network type (5G/LTE/4G/3G)?"
      ]
    },
    {
      "step": "Check SIM status",
      "why": "If the SIM isn’t detected or is locked, the phone can’t register on the network.",
      "instructions": [
        "Go to Settings > About phone > SIM status (or similar).",
        "Look for SIM state/result: Active, Missing, or Locked (PIN/PUK)."
      ],
      "if_results": {
        "Missing": [
          "Power the phone off.",
          "Eject the SIM tray, remove and reinsert the SIM carefully (gold contacts down, aligned), then reinsert the tray.",
          "Power the phone back on and check the status bar again."
