messages.content:
{
  "acknowledgement": "Thanks for checking. Your phone reporting “No SIM card detected” explains both “No Signal” and “Data Disabled.” Until the SIM is detected, the phone can’t register on the network, so MMS (and data) won’t work.",
  "thought_process": "A missing-SIM status is usually a seating/contact issue (loose SIM, dust, misaligned tray). The fastest fix is to power down and reseat the SIM so the modem can read it. If reseating doesn’t help, we’ll isolate whether the problem is the SIM card itself or the phone’s SIM slot.",
  "next_steps": [
    {
      "step": "Power off and reseat the SIM",
      "why": "Reseating resolves most ‘SIM missing’ cases by restoring proper contact.",
      "instructions": [
        "Power the phone OFF completely.",
        "Use the SIM eject tool or a small paperclip to eject the SIM tray.",
        "Remove the SIM. Check orientation so the notched corner matches the tray.",
        "Gently wipe the SIM’s gold contacts with a clean, dry microfiber cloth (no liquids).",
        "Place the SIM flat in the tray (no tilt), then slide the tray back in fully and flush.",
        "Power the phone ON and wait 30–60 seconds."
      ],
      "what_to_check_after_boot": [
        "Status bar: do you now see signal bars and a network type (5G/LTE/4G/3G)?",
        "SIM status: does it now show Active instead of Missing?"
      ]
    },
    {
      "step": "If still shows Missing after reseat",
      "why": "We need to determine whether the issue is the SIM card or the phone’s SIM slot.",
      "instructions": [
        "If available, try your SIM in another compatible phone. Does that phone detect the SIM?",
        "Or try a known‑working SIM from a friend/family member in your phone. Does your phone detect that SIM?",
        "Inspect the SIM tray for bends/cracks and ensure it sits fully flush when inserted."
      ],
      "how_to_interpret": {
        "sim_detected_in_other_phone": "Your SIM works; likely a SIM slot/tray issue in your phone.",
        "other_sim_detected_in_your_phone": "Your phone/slot is OK; your SIM card may be faulty and needs replacement.",
        "neither_detected": "Could be both SIM and slot or a deeper hardware issue; we’ll arrange support."
      }
    },
    {
      "step": "If SIM becomes Active",
      "why": "Once the network sees your SIM, data and MMS should work again (we already refueled 2 GB).",
      "instructions": [
        "Ensure Mobile Data is ON (Settings > Mobile networks > Mobile data = ON).",
        "Confirm Network mode is 4G/5G Preferred.",
        "With Wi‑Fi OFF, try loading a webpage.",
        "Then retry sending your MMS."
      ],
      "what_to_report": [
        "Did the webpage load over mobile data?",
        "Did the MMS send successfully?"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "important_notes": [
    "If the SIM status shows Locked (PIN/PUK) at any point, stop and tell me—that requires security assistance.",
    "Handle the SIM and tray gently; don’t force the tray if it isn’t aligned."
  ],
  "what_i_need_from_you": "Please reseat the SIM (Step 1) and let me know: (a) does the SIM status change to Active, (b) do you see signal bars/network type, and (c) whether mobile data/MMS work after that. If it still says Missing, tell me if you can try the cross‑test in Step 2. Based on your results, I’ll either proceed with MMS checks or arrange the right support (including SIM replacement if needed)."
}

