{
  "message": "Great progress—now that you’re on 5G, MMS should work once a few phone settings are aligned. We’ll go step by step. None of these steps delete any photos or messages; they only affect connectivity.",
  "why_these_steps": [
    "Some phones block MMS while roaming if Wi‑Fi Calling is ON.",
    "If Data Saver is ON or a VPN is active, MMS can stall.",
    "Incorrect APN/MMSC settings are a common MMS cause; resetting APN + a reboot fixes this."
  ],
  "steps_on_your_Samsung": [
    {
      "step": "Turn Wi‑Fi Calling OFF",
      "path": "Settings > Connections > Wi‑Fi Calling > OFF",
      "note": "This avoids conflicts for MMS while roaming."
    },
    {
      "step": "Make sure Data Saver is OFF",
      "path": "Settings > Connections > Data usage > Data saver > OFF",
      "note": "Data Saver can block messaging data in the background."
    },
    {
      "step": "Ensure no VPN is active",
      "path": "Settings > Connections > More connection settings > VPN > Disconnect any VPN",
      "what_to_look_for": "If you see a key icon in the status bar, a VPN is active—disconnect it."
    },
    {
      "step": "Reset APN to default (fixes MMSC settings)",
      "path": "Settings > Connections > Mobile networks > Access Point Names > menu (⋮) > Reset to default",
      "after": "After resetting, restart the phone: hold Power > Restart."
    },
    {
      "step": "After reboot, verify these toggles",
      "checks": [
        "Mobile data: ON (Settings > Connections > Data usage > Mobile data > ON)",
        "Data roaming: ON (Settings > Connections > Mobile networks > Data roaming > ON)",
        "Wi‑Fi: OFF for the test"
      ],
      "network_indicator": "Confirm you still see 4G/LTE/5G next to the signal bars."
    },
    {
      "step": "Test MMS",
      "how": "Open your Messages app and send a photo to your own number or a contact. Watch for it to show Sent.",
      "note": "Keep Wi‑Fi OFF during this test so MMS uses mobile data."
    }
    ],
  "if_it_still_fails_after_those": [
    {
      "step": "Check messaging app permissions",
      "path": "Settings > Apps > Messages (Samsung Messages or Google Messages) > Permissions",
      "ensure": [
        "Photos and videos or Storage: Allowed",
        "SMS: Allowed"
      ],
      "also_check": "In the same app screen > Mobile data or Data usage > Allow background data usage: ON"
    },
    {
      "step": "Try sending a new photo again with Wi‑Fi OFF",
      "note": "If there’s any error message, tell me exactly what it says."
    }
  ],
  "request": "Please go through the steps in order. Let me know: 1) whether Wi‑Fi Calling was ON or OFF, 2) if Data Saver or a VPN was ON, 3) that APN was reset and the phone restarted, and 4) what you see next to the signal bars after reboot (e.g., 4G/5G). Then tell me if the test picture message sends successfully."
}

