{
  "message": "Great job reseating the SIM—seeing bars is a big step forward. Because it says 2G, MMS likely won’t work yet (2G is too slow). Let’s safely switch your phone to prefer 4G/5G and make sure Mobile Data and Data Roaming are ON. Then we’ll test a picture.",
  "thought_process": "Your line is active and roaming-enabled on our side. Now that the phone sees the SIM, it’s connected on 2G, which usually can’t handle MMS. Changing the preferred network to 4G/5G and enabling data roaming on the phone should get you usable data for MMS.",
  "steps": [
    {
      "title": "Keep Wi‑Fi OFF just for testing",
      "why": "We want to be sure mobile data is working on the local network in France."
    },
    {
      "title": "Set network mode to 4G/5G preferred",
      "why": "2G is insufficient for MMS. 4G/LTE or 5G is recommended.",
      "iphone": "Settings > Cellular (or Mobile Data) > Cellular Data Options > Voice & Data > choose 5G Auto (or LTE).",
      "android": "Settings > Network & Internet (or Connections) > Mobile network (or SIMs) > Preferred network type > select 4G/5G (LTE/5G)."
    },
    {
      "title": "Turn Mobile Data ON and Data Roaming ON",
      "why": "MMS uses mobile data, and while abroad you must allow data roaming on the phone.",
      "iphone": "Settings > Cellular (Mobile Data) > Cellular Data = ON. Then Cellular Data Options > Data Roaming = ON.",
      "android": "Settings > Network & Internet (or Connections) > Mobile network (or SIMs) > Mobile Data = ON and Data Roaming = ON."
    },
    {
      "title": "Wait 20–30 seconds and check the top of the screen",
      "what_to_see": "Ideally it changes from 2G to 4G/LTE/5G. If it still shows 2G, move near a window or step outside for 30–60 seconds to let it latch onto a faster network."
    },
    {
      "title": "Quick test of mobile data",
      "how": "With Wi‑Fi OFF, open your browser and try loading example.com. If it loads, data works."
    },
    {
      "title": "Test MMS",
      "how": "Send one small photo to yourself or a contact. Watch for it to send without error."
    }
