      "case": "Still stuck on 2G or MMS won’t send",
      "try": [
        "Turn OFF Wi‑Fi Calling temporarily (some networks don’t support MMS over Wi‑Fi Calling when roaming).",
        "iPhone: Settings > Phone > Wi‑Fi Calling > Off.",
        "Android: Settings > Network & Internet (or Connections) > Mobile network (or SIMs) > Wi‑Fi Calling > Off."
      ]
    },
    {
      "case": "If MMS still fails after the above on 4G/LTE",
      "try": [
        "Reset APN to default (this restores the correct MMSC for MMS), then restart the phone.",
        "iPhone: Settings > Cellular > Cellular Data Network > tap Reset Settings (if available); otherwise tell me and I’ll guide further.",
        "Android: Settings > Mobile network > Access Point Names > menu > Reset to default. Then restart the phone and try sending a picture again."
      ]
    }
  ],
  "reassurance": "These changes are safe and reversible. They won’t erase anything—just how your phone connects to the network.",
  "what_to_report_back": [
    "After changing the network mode, what does the top of the screen show now (4G/LTE/5G or still 2G)?",
    "Could you load a webpage with Wi‑Fi OFF?",
    "Did the picture message send, or did you see any error?",
    "If you’re unsure whether it’s iPhone or Android, tell me what you see in Settings (e.g., do you see ‘Cellular’ or ‘Network & Internet’), and I’ll tailor exact taps."
  ]
}

