messages.content:
{
  "summary": "Data and 5G are working, so MMS is likely being blocked by settings on the device: missing/incorrect MMSC, Data Saver/VPN, or app permissions. You already reset APN and rebooted—great. Let’s verify the remaining items step by step.",
  "why_these_steps": "MMS uses the MMSC via your APN. If MMSC is missing/incorrect or if Data Saver/VPN/app permissions block the messaging app, MMS won’t send even though web browsing works.",
  "steps_now": [
    {
      "step": "Confirm the MMSC is now present after the APN reset",
      "actions": [
        "Run check_apn_settings.",
        "Tell me the APN name and whether an MMSC URL is shown (include the URL if present)."
      ],
      "reason": "We need to ensure the reset actually populated the MMSC. If it’s still missing, that’s the primary blocker."
    },
    {
      "step": "Turn off any data restrictions",
      "actions": [
        "Run check_data_restriction_status.",
        "If it reports Data Saver is ON, run toggle_data_saver_mode to turn it OFF."
      ],
      "reason": "Data Saver can interfere with MMS traffic."
    },
    {
      "step": "Eliminate VPN interference",
      "actions": [
        "Run check_vpn_status.",
        "If a VPN is connected, run disconnect_vpn."
      ],
      "reason": "Some VPNs block or slow MMS traffic."
    },
    {
      "step": "Ensure the messaging app has required permissions",
      "actions": [
        "Run check_app_permissions(app_name=\"messaging\").",
        "If Storage or SMS is not granted, run grant_app_permission(app_name=\"messaging\", permission=\"storage\") and grant_app_permission(app_name=\"messaging\", permission=\"sms\")."
      ],
      "reason": "Without Storage and SMS permissions, MMS can fail."
    },
    {
      "step": "Quick capability test",
      "actions": [
        "Run can_send_mms and share the result.",
        "Then, with Wi‑Fi OFF and Mobile Data + Data Roaming ON, try sending a small photo MMS to a single contact again."
      ],
      "reason": "This confirms whether the device now sees MMS as ready to send."
    }
  ],
  "optional_app_specific_check": {
    "instructions": [
      "If you’re on Android, open Settings > Apps > [Your messaging app] > Mobile data and ensure Background data is allowed and Allow data usage while Data Saver is on is enabled.",
      "If another messaging app is available (e.g., Google Messages vs. the phone’s default), try sending one MMS from the other app to rule out an app-specific issue."
    ]
  },
  "please_report_back_with": [
    "APN name and whether MMSC is now present (and the MMSC URL if shown).",
    "Whether Data Saver was ON and if you turned it OFF.",
    "Whether a VPN was connected and if you disconnected it.",
    "Whether Storage and SMS permissions are granted to your messaging app.",
    "Result of can_send_mms and the new MMS send attempt."
  ],
  "next_if_needed": "If the MMSC is still missing after an APN reset and reboot, that likely requires carrier provisioning assistance. I’ll escalate to a human agent at that point. If MMSC is present and all restrictions/permissions are correct but MMS still fails, we’ll try another messaging app to isolate the issue and then escalate if necessary."
}

